/*
Problem: Valid Anagram
Link: https://leetcode.com/problems/valid-anagram/

Approach:
- If the lengths of both strings are different, they cannot be anagrams.
- Use a frequency array of size 26 to store character counts.
- Increase the count for characters of string s.
- Decrease the count for characters of string t.
- If all frequencies become zero, both strings have the same characters with the same frequency.

Mistake & Learning:
- Initially, I used find() and erase() functions to remove matching characters from the string.
- Learned that find() searches the first occurrence of a character/string and returns its index.
- Learned that erase() removes characters from a string using index and count.
- Learned that frequency counting is more efficient than searching and deleting characters repeatedly.
*/

class Solution {
public:
    bool isAnagram(string s, string t) {
        if (s.size() != t.size()) {
            return false;
        }

        int freq[26] = {0};

        for (int i = 0; i < s.size(); i++) {
            freq[s[i] - 'a']++;
            freq[t[i] - 'a']--;
        }

        for (int i = 0; i < 26; i++) {
            if (freq[i] != 0) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }
};

/*
Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)

Possible Optimization:
- For larger character sets, use unordered_map instead of a fixed frequency array.
*/
